  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)z+8=1\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3)z+8 & =1 \\\\ -7(k+3)z+8-8 & =1-8 \\\\ {{-7(k+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-7}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-7(k+3)}{-7} & =\\frac{0}{-7} \\\\ k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
